# Update docs with feature changes

When you change player-facing pack behavior (recipes, items, spawners, condensing, commands), update `docs/` in the **same** work. Source of truth is the tables in `tools/generate_datapack.py` (`CONDENSED`, `SPAWNERS`), not the generated `datapack/` tree.

## Files

| File | Update when |
| --- | --- |
| `docs/existing-spawner-support.md` | A spawner recipe is added, removed, or its ingredients/pattern change |

Keep the docs concise (ids + custom condensed items). Mirror `C` / `SC` and Iron Bars notes already used there.

Do **not** skip docs because README also lists recipes. If `docs/` has no file for the kind of change (e.g. condensing-only), add a short note to the closest existing doc or ask before creating a new file.

Docs-only edits do not require a version bump.
